# Tailwind CSS Guidelines

## Core Configuration (v4)

- **CSS-First Config**: Use `@theme` directive instead of `tailwind.config.js`.
- **Import Syntax**: Use `@import "tailwindcss"` instead of `@tailwind` directives.
- **Package Names**: Use `@tailwindcss/postcss`, `@tailwindcss/cli`, and `@tailwindcss/vite`.

### Example Configuration
```css
@import "tailwindcss";

@theme {
  --font-display: "Satoshi", "sans-serif";
  --breakpoint-3xl: 1920px;
  --color-avocado-500: oklch(0.84 0.18 117.33);
  --ease-fluid: cubic-bezier(0.3, 0, 0, 1);

  /* Override defaults */
  --font-*: initial;
}
```

## Best Practices

### 1. Utility-First Workflow
- **Avoid custom CSS** whenever possible. Use Tailwind utilities for almost everything.
- **Don't mix styles**: Avoid using `style={{ ... }}` attributes unless for dynamic values that can't be classes (like specific coordinates).

### 2. Mobile-First Design
- Write styles for mobile first, then add breakpoints for larger screens.
- Avoid `max-w` breakpoints unless absolutely necessary.

```html
<!-- ❌ BAD: Desktop first -->
<div class="w-1/2 max-md:w-full">

<!-- ✅ GOOD: Mobile first -->
<div class="w-full md:w-1/2">
```

### 3. Dynamic Classes
- **NEVER construct class names dynamically**. Tailwind's scanner cannot detect them.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD
const color = "red";
<div className={`bg-${color}-500`} /> // Tailwind won't generate bg-red-500

// ✅ GOOD
const colorClasses = {
  red: "bg-red-500",
  blue: "bg-blue-500",
};
<div className={colorClasses[color]} />
```

### 4. Class Merging
- Use `clsx` and `tailwind-merge` (via the `cn` utility) to conditionally apply and merge classes.
- This handles conflicts correctly (e.g., `p-4` vs `p-8`).

```tsx
import { cn } from "@/lib/utils";

// ✅ GOOD
<div className={cn("p-4 bg-red-500", isActive && "bg-blue-500", className)} />
```

### 5. Component Reusability vs @apply
- **Prefer React Components** over `@apply` for reusability.
- Use `@apply` *only* when you need to override 3rd party styles or targeting specific sub-elements not accessible via props.

```css
/* ❌ Avoid overuse of @apply */
.btn {
  @apply px-4 py-2 bg-blue-500 rounded;
}
```

```tsx
/* ✅ Prefer Component Composition */
function Button({ className, ...props }) {
  return <button className={cn("px-4 py-2 bg-blue-500 rounded", className)} {...props} />;
}
```

### 6. Accessibility (a11y)
- Use `sr-only` for text that should be visible only to screen readers.
- Use `focus-visible:*` utilities for keyboard navigation focus states.

```html
<button class="focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-none">
  <span class="sr-only">Close menu</span>
  <XIcon />
</button>
```

### 7. Ordering & Organization
- Use `prettier-plugin-tailwindcss` to automatically sort classes.
- Group related variants (e.g., keep all `hover:` classes together if manual sorting is needed, but rely on the plugin).

## New Features (v4)

### Container Queries
Use `@container` to style elements based on their parent's size.

```html
<div class="@container">
  <div class="@sm:text-lg @md:text-xl">
    Responsive to container
  </div>
</div>
```

### 3D Transforms
Use native 3D transform utilities.

```html
<div class="transform-3d rotate-x-12 rotate-y-6 perspective-distant">
  3D Element
</div>
```

### Enhanced Gradients
New syntax for linear gradients.

```html
<div class="bg-linear-45 from-blue-500 to-purple-500">
  45-degree gradient
</div>
```

### Composable Variants
Chain variants for complex logic.

```html
<div class="group">
  <span class="group-has-data-active:group-hover:opacity-100">
    Visible when parent has data-active AND is hovered
  </span>
</div>
```

### CSS Variables in Arbitrary Values
New syntax uses parenthesis `()` instead of brackets `[]`.

```html
<!-- v4 Syntax -->
<div class="bg-(--brand-color)">
```
